_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2482:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-059.json:3:  "prompt": "# T-059 — Pipeline Kanban view UI\n\nPRD: docs/prd/01-NPD-PRD.md §17.8, §17.12 + UX prototypes/design/01-NPD-UX.md pipeline_kanban\nProject root: /Users/mariuszkrawczyk/Projects/monopilot-kira\nPrototype: prototypes/design/Monopilot Design System/npd/pipeline.jsx:19-52 (KanbanCard + KanbanView)\n\n## Goal\nClient component KanbanView rendering 6 columns (G0-G4 + Launched) with project cards, drag-and-drop adjacency-guarded via @dnd-kit/core, optimistic UI revert on 422 ADJACENCY_VIOLATION. Mounted at /(npd)/pipeline?view=kanban (default).\n\n## Implementation contract\n1. apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_components/kanban-view.tsx ('use client') uses @dnd-kit/core; renders shadcn Card per project; column header per gate with count.\n2. onDragEnd calls advanceProjectGate(projectId, targetGate) — optimistic update + rollback on error.\n3. Card content matches prototype: code, name, prio badge, owner, target_launch.\n4. RTL test asserts 6 columns + card rendering + DnD adjacency rejection (mock action returns 422).\n\n## Files\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/page.tsx [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_components/kanban-view.tsx [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_components/kanban-card.tsx [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_components/__tests__/kanban-view.test.tsx [create]\n- prototypes/design/Monopilot Design System/npd/pipeline.jsx [ref]\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given the production page renders, when compared to prototypes/design/Monopilot Design System/npd/pipeline.jsx:19-52 (KanbanCard + KanbanView), then it has 6 gate columns (G0,G1,G2,G3,G4,Launched), KanbanCard with code+name+prio badge+owner+target_launch, and uses @dnd-kit/core + shadcn Card primitives — verified by RTL snapshot + parity checklist\n2. Given a card is dragged from G2 to G3 (adjacent), when drop fires, then advanceProjectGate is invoked with targetGate=G3 and UI updates optimistically per §17.12 adjacency rule\n3. Given the action returns 422 ADJACENCY_VIOLATION, when the drop completes, then the card snaps back to its source column and a toast shows the error per §17.12 optimistic-revert contract\n\n## Test strategy\n- RED: RTL test asserting 6 columns + card content + DnD adjacent + 422 revert before component exists\n- Run 'pnpm --filter web test kanban-view'\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not allow non-adjacent drop without server validation\n- Do not paste prototype JSX verbatim — translate to @dnd-kit + shadcn\n- Do not skip optimistic revert UX",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2507:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-062.json:3:  "prompt": "# T-062 — Stage-Gate end-to-end\n\nPRD: docs/prd/01-NPD-PRD.md §17.6, §17.7\nProject root: /Users/mariuszkrawczyk/Projects/monopilot-kira\n\n## Goal\nPlaywright E2E covering full project lifecycle: NPD Manager creates project → kanban view → tick required items → advance G0→G1→G2 → request G3 approval → e-sign with password → assert gate_approvals row + esign_hash + outbox events emitted in order.\n\n## Implementation contract\n1. apps/web/e2e/npd/stage-gate.spec.ts: login as NPD Manager → /(npd)/pipeline → click + new → fill wizard → submit → assert kanban shows new project at G0 → tick checklist items → drag to G1 → drag to G2 → click 'Request Approval' → e-sign with password → assert success.\n2. Integration test apps/web/__tests__/integration/gate-events.test.ts: verifies outbox events emitted in order npd.project.created → npd.gate.advanced (×2) → npd.gate.approved.\n3. Fixtures seed deterministic project state (no checklists pre-seeded).\n\n## Files\n- apps/web/e2e/npd/stage-gate.spec.ts [create]\n- apps/web/__tests__/integration/gate-events.test.ts [create]\n- apps/web/e2e/npd/fixtures/stage-gate-seed.ts [create]\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given an NPD Manager session, when the user creates a project then advances it from G0 to G3 via the UI then approves with password, then a gate_approvals row exists with decision='approved' + non-null esign_hash + esigned_at per §17.6 e-sig flow\n2. Given the project lifecycle completes, when the outbox table is queried, then events appear in order: npd.project.created → npd.gate.advanced (G0→G1) → npd.gate.advanced (G1→G2) → npd.gate.advanced (G2→G3) → npd.gate.approved per §17.6\n3. Given an attempt to drag from G2 to G4 (non-adjacent), when drop fires, then the card snaps back and a toast 'Adjacency violation' appears per §17.12 adjacency guard\n\n## Test strategy\n- RED: write the 3 specs above before final wiring; run against isolated test container\n- Run 'pnpm --filter web test:e2e stage-gate && pnpm --filter web test gate-events'\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not skip outbox event ordering assertion\n- Do not run against shared/staging DB\n- Do not embed real secrets in test password (use fixture)\n\n## 2026-05-03 E2E spine patch — extend to full release path\nExtend this E2E beyond G3 approval to the canonical spine:\nBrief creation → linked project at G0 → G0/G1/G2 → G3 create/map FG candidate → department closure evidence → G4 approval/preflight → NPD Builder release dry-run or real test release → Technical approval dependency visible → release status/read model asserted.\n\nThis test must verify that D365 disabled does not block Monopilot release and that D365 export does not set factory release state.",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2604:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-096.json:3:  "prompt": "# T-096 — releaseNpdProjectToFactory canonical NPD Builder release transaction\n\nPRD: docs/prd/01-NPD-PRD.md final decisions + 2026-05-03 E2E release spike\nProject root: /Users/mariuszkrawczyk/Projects/monopilot-kira\n\n## Goal\nAdd the canonical `releaseNpdProjectToFactory(projectId)` / `executeNpdBuilderRelease(projectId)` domain action that ties Stage-Gate G4, department closure, FG mapping, shared BOM SSOT, RM usability, factory_spec creation and release status into one idempotent NPD Builder release transaction.\n\n## Implementation contract\nPreconditions:\n- project exists, has linked Brief, and current gate allows G4 release;\n- FG candidate mapped by T-095;\n- required 7-department Done_<Dept> closures are present per T-056 matrix;\n- Settings approval policy is satisfied;\n- risk/docs blockers clear where configured;\n- RM usability PASS for every BOM component via Technical T-074 service/read model;\n- Technical approval is required for factory_spec/BOM factory use.\n\nTransaction outputs:\n- WIP/intermediate item rows and confirmed FG item mapping;\n- initial shared BOM header/lines by invoking T-093/T-092 SSOT writer;\n- initial factory_spec draft or in_review through Technical T-079 API;\n- release audit row/outbox events;\n- release status from T-097 set to `pending_technical_approval` unless already approved by a valid Technical approval workflow.\n\nD365 export is explicitly out-of-transaction and optional.",
