specs above before final wiring; run against isolated test container\n- Run 'pnpm --filter web test:e2e stage-gate && pnpm --filter web test gate-events'\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not skip outbox event ordering assertion\n- Do not run against shared/staging DB\n- Do not embed real secrets in test password (use fixture)\n\n## 2026-05-03 E2E spine patch — extend to full release path\nExtend this E2E beyond G3 approval to the canonical spine:\nBrief creation → linked project at G0 → G0/G1/G2 → G3 create/map FG candidate → department closure evidence → G4 approval/preflight → NPD Builder release dry-run or real test release → Technical approval dependency visible → release status/read model asserted.\n\nThis test must verify that D365 disabled does not block Monopilot release and that D365 export does not set factory release state.",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2612:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-058.json:2:  "title": "T-058 — advanceProjectGate + approveProjectGate (e-sig) + revertGate Server Actions (NPD-f) [PATCH: G3/G4 blockers]",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2613:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-058.json:3:  "prompt": "# T-058 — Gate advancement + approval Server Actions\n\nPRD: docs/prd/01-NPD-PRD.md §17.6, §17.7, §17.12 (adjacency guard)\nProject root: /Users/mariuszkrawczyk/Projects/monopilot-kira\n\n## Goal\nThree Server Actions enforcing gate advancement: advanceProjectGate (G0-G2 self-advance with blocker check), approveProjectGate (G3/G4 with bcrypt-verified password + e-signature SHA-256 hash + audit immutability), revertGate (admin-only audit-logged reverse).\n\n## Implementation contract\n1. apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/advance-project-gate.ts: RBAC npd.gate.advance; calls getBlockers helper; applies adjacency guard nextGate(current) only; updates current_gate; emits 'npd.gate.advanced'.\n2. apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/approve-project-gate.ts: RBAC npd.gate.approve; takes {decision, notes, password}; verifies password via bcrypt against current user; on approve writes gate_approvals row with esigned_at + esign_hash=SHA-256(user_id+project_id+gate+timestamp); advances current_gate; emits 'npd.gate.approved'.\n3. apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/revert-gate.ts: RBAC admin only; writes audit_events; emits 'npd.gate.reverted'.\n4. Vitest covers blocker-rejection, adjacency violation (422 ADJACENCY_VIOLATION), password mismatch reject, hash determinism, and audit-event emission.\n\n## Files\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/advance-project-gate.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/approve-project-gate.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/revert-gate.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/_lib/gate-helpers.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/__tests__/gate-actions.test.ts [create]\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given a project at G2 with one required checklist item not done, when advanceProjectGate to G3 is called, then it rejects with BLOCKERS_PRESENT and current_gate stays G2 per §17.6 blocker rule\n2. Given a project at G2, when advanceProjectGate to G4 (non-adjacent) is called, then it rejects 422 ADJACENCY_VIOLATION per §17.12 adjacency guard\n3. Given approveProjectGate is called with correct password, when commit succeeds, then gate_approvals row contains esign_hash matching SHA-256(user_id + project_id + gate_code + esigned_at) per §17.5 + §17.6 e-sig contract\n\n## Test strategy\n- RED: __tests__/gate-actions.test.ts with 4 cases (blocker reject, adjacency reject, password reject, hash determinism + audit emit) before actions exist\n- Run 'pnpm --filter web test gate-actions'\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not skip blocker check\n- Do not allow non-adjacent advance (per §17.12)\n- Do not store the password in any column or log\n- Do not skip audit_events emission on revertGate\n\n## 2026-05-03 E2E spine patch — G3/G4 advancement blockers\nGate actions must call the E2E blocker helpers added by T-095/T-096/T-097:\n- G3 approval/advance is blocked unless an FG candidate is created or mapped (`npd_projects.product_code` or equivalent) and is unique to this active project.\n- G4 approval is blocked unless required department closures are Done, release preflight passes, RM usability has no blocking FAIL, shared BOM/factory_spec handoff is ready, and Settings policy approvals are satisfied.\n- G4 approval may close NPD, but factory use remains blocked until Technical approval sets the release status/read model to approved/released per T-097.\n- D365 export must not satisfy or mutate any gate blocker.",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2616:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-058.json:31:    "details": "advanceProjectGate enforces blocker + adjacency. approveProjectGate verifies password via bcrypt then writes gate_approvals + esign_hash. revertGate is admin-only and audit-logged. Helper getBlockers + nextGate factored.\nPreserved acceptance requirements: Given a project at G2 with no FG candidate, when approve/advance to G3 is called, then it rejects with FG_CANDIDATE_REQUIRED.; Given a project at G3 with any required department not Done, when approveProjectGate for G4 is called, then it rejects with DEPARTMENT_CLOSURE_REQUIRED and typed blockers.; Given D365 export exists but Technical approval is missing, when factory release blockers are evaluated, then the project is not released_to_factory.",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2618:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-058.json:54:      "Given a project at G2, when advanceProjectGate to G4 (non-adjacent) is called, then it rejects 422 ADJACENCY_VIOLATION per §17.12 adjacency guard",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2620:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-054.json:3:  "prompt": "# T-054 — Stage-Gate core tables\n\nPRD: docs/prd/01-NPD-PRD.md §17.3, §17.4, §17.5\nProject root: /Users/mariuszkrawczyk/Projects/monopilot-kira\n\n## Goal\nCreate the three foundational Stage-Gate tables (npd_projects, gate_checklist_items, gate_approvals) with R13 audit columns + RLS + indexes per §17.3-§17.5 DDL.\n\n## Implementation contract\n1. Migration packages/db/migrations/0054_npd_projects_and_gates.sql per PRD §17.3-§17.5 DDL exactly: npd_projects (UUID PK, code UNIQUE, current_gate G0..G4|Launched, current_stage, prio, owner, target_launch, product_code FK fa, R13 audit cols), gate_checklist_items (UUID PK, project_id ON DELETE CASCADE, gate_code, category_code, item_text, required, completed_at, completed_by_user, evidence_file), gate_approvals (UUID PK, project_id, gate_code, decision in approved/rejected, approver_user_id, esigned_at, esign_hash).\n2. Indexes: gate_checklist_items (tenant_id, project_id, gate_code) + gate_approvals (tenant_id, project_id, gate_code).\n3. ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY + tenant_isolation policies on all three tables.\n4. Drizzle schemas in packages/db/src/schema/npd-projects.ts + gate-checklist-items.ts + gate-approvals.ts; barrel updated.\n\n## Files\n- packages/db/migrations/0054_npd_projects_and_gates.sql [create]\n- packages/db/src/schema/npd-projects.ts [create]\n- packages/db/src/schema/gate-checklist-items.ts [create]\n- packages/db/src/schema/gate-approvals.ts [create]\n- packages/db/src/schema/index.ts [modify]\n- packages/db/__tests__/npd-projects-and-gates.test.ts [create]\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given migration 0054 runs, when \\d npd_projects runs, then it lists code (UNIQUE), current_gate, current_stage, prio, owner, target_launch, product_code FK fa(product_code), and R13 audit cols (created_at, created_by_user, app_version, schema_version) per §17.3 DDL\n2. Given an npd_projects row exists, when DELETE on it runs, then matching gate_checklist_items rows are CASCADE-deleted but gate_approvals rows are retained per §17.4 vs §17.5 DDL (CASCADE only on checklist_items)\n3. Given two tenants seeded, when tenant A SELECT * FROM gate_approvals runs, then it returns only tenant A rows (RLS verified)\n\n## Test strategy\n- RED: write packages/db/__tests__/npd-projects-and-gates.test.ts asserting schema shape + cascade rules + RLS isolation before migration exists\n- Run 'pnpm --filter db migrate && pnpm --filter db test npd-projects-and-gates'\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not omit ON DELETE CASCADE on gate_checklist_items (per §17.4 DDL)\n- Do not allow ON DELETE CASCADE on gate_approvals (audit immutable)\n- Do not skip RLS on any of the three tables",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2627:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-100.json:2:  "title": "T-100 — Stage-Gate G4 Launched closeout + Trial/Pilot/Handoff/Packaging LEGACY successor mapping (NPD-f §17.11.6)",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2628:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-100.json:3:  "prompt": "# T-100 — Stage-Gate G4 Launched closeout + LEGACY successor mapping\n\nPRD: docs/prd/01-NPD-PRD.md §17.11.6 (LEGACY notes [BL-NPD-02]), §17.2 (Gate definitions), §17.6 (Gate advancement flow), §17.12 (Pipeline View Modes G4→Launched arrow)\nProject root: /Users/mariuszkrawczyk/Projects/monopilot-kira\nPrototype: prototypes/design/Monopilot Design System/npd/stage-gate-screens.jsx (pipeline kanban — Launched column)\n\n## Goal\nWhen an NPD project advances from G4 to `Launched`, formally close out the four legacy R&D stages (Trial, Pilot, Handoff, Packaging) by writing successor-anchor evidence rows that bind each legacy stage to its canonical successor location per the §17.11.6 migration map. This task closes the coverage.md note: \"§17.11.6 LEGACY (Trial/Pilot/Handoff/Packaging) is not deprecated. These stages return as part of NPD and must be represented in Stage-Gate flow coverage\" — currently no task creates the binding rows.\n\n## Migration map (§17.11.6, authoritative)\n\n| Legacy stage | Successor location bound on G4→Launched |\n|---|---|\n| Trial    | `product.shelf_life` set + allergens cascade recomputed for current `bom_header_id` |\n| Pilot    | First Production WO created against the released FG (08-PRODUCTION T-016..T-022 contract) recorded as `npd_project_pilot_wo_id` |\n| Handoff  | Stage-Gate G4 e-sign event (T-124 e-sign primitive) + initial shared BOM version (T-093) both present and approved-for-factory |\n| Packaging| Brief packaging cols C14–C19 frozen-copy snapshotted onto the released FG; MRP dept marked complete |\n\n## Implementation contract\n1. New DB migration `packages/db/migrations/00xx_npd_legacy_closeout.sql` adds table `npd_legacy_closeout`:\n   - `id uuid PK`, `org_id uuid NOT NULL` (RLS via `app.current_org_id()`), `npd_project_id uuid NOT NULL FK`, `fg_product_code text NOT NULL`, `closed_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()`, `closed_by uuid NOT NULL`, `release_event_id uuid NOT NULL FK -> outbox events`,\n   - `trial_shelf_life_set boolean`, `trial_allergens_cascade_recomputed_at timestamptz`,\n   - `pilot_wo_id uuid NULL FK -> production wo (soft FK; cross-module 08-PROD)`,\n   - `handoff_g4_esign_id uuid NOT NULL FK -> e_sign_events`, `handoff_bom_header_id uuid NOT NULL FK -> bom_headers`,\n   - `packaging_snapshot_jsonb jsonb NOT NULL`, `packaging_mrp_complete boolean NOT NULL`,\n   - UNIQUE(npd_project_id) — one closeout row per project; ENABLE+FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY; R13 audit cols.\n2. New Server Action `apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/close-out-legacy-stages.ts` invoked by the existing G4→Launched gate transition (T-058 advanceGate API):\n   - Reads project + FG release state (T-097), validates approved_for_factory, validates G4 e-sign exists, snapshots Brief C14–C19, writes one `npd_legacy_closeout` row in a single tx, emits `npd.project.legacy_stages_closed` outbox event with the four successor anchor IDs.\n   - On any precondition failure: returns typed error code (`TRIAL_SHELF_LIFE_MISSING` | `PILOT_WO_NOT_LINKED` | `HANDOFF_BOM_NOT_APPROVED` | `PACKAGING_MRP_INCOMPLETE`) and does NOT advance gate; gate transition rolls back.\n3. Pipeline UI (§17.12 kanban Launched column) shows a closeout-status pill on each Launched card with 4 sub-indicators (Trial / Pilot / Handoff / Packaging) reading from the `npd_legacy_closeout` row; missing successor anchors render as warning chip with the typed error code from step 2.\n\n## Files\n- packages/db/migrations/00xx_npd_legacy_closeout.sql [create]\n- packages/db/src/schema/npd-legacy-closeout.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/close-out-legacy-stages.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/__tests__/close-out-legacy-stages.test.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_components/launched-card-closeout-pill.tsx [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_components/__tests__/launched-card-closeout-pill.test.tsx [create]\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given an NPD project at G4 with approved-for-factory release state, valid G4 e-sign, linked Pilot WO id, frozen Brief C14-C19 snapshot and MRP=complete, when an authorized user advances the gate to Launched, then exactly one `npd_legacy_closeout` row is inserted with all four successor anchor IDs populated and the `npd.project.legacy_stages_closed` outbox event is emitted with those IDs per §17.11.6 migration map.\n2. Given a G4 project missing the Pilot WO link, when the user advances to Launched, then the Server Action returns typed error `PILOT_WO_NOT_LINKED`, the gate stays at G4, no `npd_legacy_closeout` row is written, and the Launched-column closeout pill renders the warning chip with the error code per §17.6 gate advancement flow.\n3. Given two simultaneous Launched transitions for the same project (race), when both attempts run, then exactly one row is created (UNIQUE(npd_project_id)) and the second attempt returns a typed `ALREADY_CLOSED` idempotent response.\n4. Given two orgs each have a project advancing to Launched, when both queries run under their own `app.current_org_id()` session, then each only sees its own closeout row (RLS verified).\n5. Given the prototype `npd/stage-gate-screens.jsx` Launched column card, when the implemented `launched-card-closeout-pill` is rendered, then it has the same 4 sub-indicator dots (Trial/Pilot/Handoff/Packaging) in the same order and colors as the prototype — verified by RTL snapshot + parity checklist per UI-PROTOTYPE-PARITY-POLICY.md.\n\n## Test strategy\n- RED 1: vitest `apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/__tests__/close-out-legacy-stages.test.ts` asserts AC 1 (happy path), AC 2 (PILOT_WO_NOT_LINKED rollback), AC 3 (race idempotency), AC 4 (RLS isolation) — fails before Server Action exists.\n- RED 2: RTL test `launched-card-closeout-pill.test.tsx` snapshots the 4 sub-indicator dots vs prototype and asserts warning chip surfacing per error code (AC 5).\n- Run `pnpm --filter db migrate && pnpm --filter web test close-out-legacy-stages && pnpm --filter web test launched-card-closeout-pill`.\n- UI evidence: attach Playwright trace and screenshot per `_meta/atomic-tasks/UI-PROTOTYPE-PARITY-POLICY.md`.\n\n## Prototype parity\nReuse the existing pipeline Launched column from `prototypes/design/Monopilot Design System/npd/stage-gate-screens.jsx`; only the closeout pill is new. Do not redesign the column header, drag-handles, card layout, or status colors — match 1:1.\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not let `Built` (D365) or D365 export alone trigger this closeout — only the real G4→Launched gate advancement (§17.11.6 successor map plus T-097 release state must be `approved_for_factory` or stronger).\n- Do not in-place mutate Brief packaging cols — packaging closeout MUST be a frozen JSONB snapshot per §17.11.6 Packaging row (post-release mutation requires a new BOM/spec version + Technical approval).\n- Do not stamp the closeout row without a real G4 e-sign event id — the handoff anchor is e-sign, not a mock or self-attestation.\n- Do not allow the Server Action to backdate `closed_at` — clock is server-side `now()` only, R13 audit row records actor + reason.\n- Do not implement gate adjacency bypass: Launched is only reachable from G4 per §17.12 adjacency guard; reverse moves are admin-only via `revertGate`.\n",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2630:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-100.json:32:    "details": "Per coverage.md: '§17.11.6 LEGACY (Trial/Pilot/Handoff/Packaging) is not deprecated. These stages return as part of NPD and must be represented in Stage-Gate flow coverage.' Currently no task creates the binding rows that prove each legacy stage's successor anchor exists at Launched. This task adds the canonical npd_legacy_closeout row written transactionally inside the existing G4→Launched gate Server Action, with a typed-error rollback path and a Launched-column UI pill surfacing the four sub-indicators. References shared BOM SSOT (T-092/T-093/T-096), factory release state (T-097), e-sign primitive (T-124 in 00-foundation), G4 gate advance (T-058), and 08-Production WO link (cross-module soft FK).",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2643:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-092.json:3:  "prompt": "# T-092 — shared BOM SSOT schema for NPD Builder initial BOM\n\nPRD: docs/prd/01-NPD-PRD.md 2026-05-03 FINAL Amendment + _meta/decisions/2026-05-03-flow-d365-settings-technical-decisions.md\nProject root: /Users/mariuszkrawczyk/Projects/monopilot-kira\n\n## Final decisions this task must implement\n- `FG` / Finished Good is canonical; `FA` is compatibility alias only.\n- Stage-Gate G0-G4 is canonical MVP. Brief creates NPD project (`DEV-123`); project creates/maps FG at G3.\n- NPD Builder creates WIP/intermediate items + FG + the initial shared BOM/product-spec version after all required department closures and approval.\n- One shared BOM table/model is SSOT across NPD, Technical, Planning, Production and integrations.\n- D365 is export/import integration only and must not be schema source of truth.\n- Released NPD product/BOM/spec edits create a new version and require Technical approval before factory use.\n\n## Goal\nExtend the existing shared BOM schema owned with Technical so NPD Builder can create the initial BOM/product-spec version in the same canonical `bom_headers`/`bom_lines` model used by Technical, Planning and Production. This is now ACTIONABLE under the final 2026-05-03 decisions; do not keep this task blocked on FA/FG or BOM SSOT clarification.\n\n## Implementation contract\n1. Inspect existing `bom_headers` and `bom_lines` schema/migrations before editing. Reuse the existing shared Technical BOM model where possible; do not create an NPD-only BOM table.\n2. Ensure `bom_headers` can represent an NPD-originated initial version:\n   - status/lifecycle supports at least `draft`, `in_review`, `technical_approved`, `active`, `superseded`, `archived` (map to existing enum names if already equivalent; document mapping in comments/tests).\n   - `origin_module` enum/string supports `npd`, `technical`, `imported` and defaults safely for existing rows.\n   - link to NPD project/legacy FA compatibility identifier for traceability (prefer `npd_project_id`; keep nullable legacy `fa_id`/`fa_code` only if already present or needed by existing code).\n   - link to released `product_id`/FG once NPD Builder creates/maps the FG.\n   - add constraints so a header cannot be orphaned: it must reference an FG/product or an NPD project/compatibility FA during pre-release.\n3. Add version fields or verify existing fields support immutable versioning (`version`, `supersedes_bom_header_id`, `effective_from`, approval timestamps/users). Do not mutate approved active versions in place.\n4. Add indexes for NPD project lookup, FG/product lookup, active version lookup and Technical approval queue lookup.\n5. Add schema comments/JSDoc stating `bom_headers/bom_lines` are shared BOM SSOT and D365 is integration only.\n6. Mark any legacy NPD computed BOM view as DEPRECATED/preview-only; do not drop it in this task. Reader switch/backfill/drop is T-093.\n7. Migration filename: `0092_shared_bom_ssot_npd_origin.sql` or next available sequence if numbering differs.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Given schema introspection after migration, when `bom_headers` is inspected, then it can store NPD-originated initial BOM versions and Technical-originated versions in the same table/model.\n- Given an NPD project before FG release, when inserting an NPD-originated draft/in_review BOM header linked to that project/compatibility FA and no product_id yet, then insert succeeds.\n- Given an orphan BOM header with neither product/FG nor NPD project/compatibility FA link, when inserted, then it fails.\n- Given a released/active BOM version exists, when a change is requested, then schema supports creating a new version/superseding relationship rather than updating the active version in place.\n- Given Technical approval fields/status are inspected, when a new post-release version is created, then it can remain non-active until Technical approval.\n- Given code comments/schema docs are grepped, then they state shared BOM is SSOT and D365 is not source of truth.\n- Given the legacy computed NPD BOM view remains, then it is clearly marked DEPRECATED/preview-only and not described as canonical.\n\n## Test strategy\n- RED schema tests for lifecycle enum/status mapping, origin_module, orphan constraint, NPD pre-release insert, released-version supersession, and Technical approval pending state.\n- Migration dry-run on fresh DB and existing fixture DB.\n- Run relevant db/schema tests plus `pnpm tsc --noEmit` if available.\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not create a second NPD BOM SSOT table.\n- Do not treat D365 import/cache tables as canonical BOM/product source.\n- Do not drop the legacy computed view in this task; only deprecate/comment it.\n- Do not mutate approved active BOM/product-spec versions in place.\n- Do not remove FA compatibility aliases/routes/views in this task.\n- Do not run in parallel with T-093 backfill/drop or any broad terminology refactor.\n",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2675:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-062.json:3:  "prompt": "# T-062 — Stage-Gate end-to-end\n\nPRD: docs/prd/01-NPD-PRD.md §17.6, §17.7\nProject root: /Users/mariuszkrawczyk/Projects/monopilot-kira\n\n## Goal\nPlaywright E2E covering full project lifecycle: NPD Manager creates project → kanban view → tick required items → advance G0→G1→G2 → request G3 approval → e-sign with password → assert gate_approvals row + esign_hash + outbox events emitted in order.\n\n## Implementation contract\n1. apps/web/e2e/npd/stage-gate.spec.ts: login as NPD Manager → /(npd)/pipeline → click + new → fill wizard → submit → assert kanban shows new project at G0 → tick checklist items → drag to G1 → drag to G2 → click 'Request Approval' → e-sign with password → assert success.\n2. Integration test apps/web/__tests__/integration/gate-events.test.ts: verifies outbox events emitted in order npd.project.created → npd.gate.advanced (×2) → npd.gate.approved.\n3. Fixtures seed deterministic project state (no checklists pre-seeded).\n\n## Files\n- apps/web/e2e/npd/stage-gate.spec.ts [create]\n- apps/web/__tests__/integration/gate-events.test.ts [create]\n- apps/web/e2e/npd/fixtures/stage-gate-seed.ts [create]\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given an NPD Manager session, when the user creates a project then advances it from G0 to G3 via the UI then approves with password, then a gate_approvals row exists with decision='approved' + non-null esign_hash + esigned_at per §17.6 e-sig flow\n2. Given the project lifecycle completes, when the outbox table is queried, then events appear in order: npd.project.created → npd.gate.advanced (G0→G1) → npd.gate.advanced (G1→G2) → npd.gate.advanced (G2→G3) → npd.gate.approved per §17.6\n3. Given an attempt to drag from G2 to G4 (non-adjacent), when drop fires, then the card snaps back and a toast 'Adjacency violation' appears per §17.12 adjacency guard\n\n## Test strategy\n- RED: write the 3 specs above before final wiring; run against isolated test container\n- Run 'pnpm --filter web test:e2e stage-gate && pnpm --filter web test gate-events'\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not skip outbox event ordering assertion\n- Do not run against shared/staging DB\n- Do not embed real secrets in test password (use fixture)\n\n## 2026-05-03 E2E spine patch — extend to full release path\nExtend this E2E beyond G3 approval to the canonical spine:\nBrief creation → linked project at G0 → G0/G1/G2 → G3 create/map FG candidate → department closure evidence → G4 approval/preflight → NPD Builder release dry-run or real test release → Technical approval dependency visible → release status/read model asserted.\n\nThis test must verify that D365 disabled does not block Monopilot release and that D365 export does not set factory release state.",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2677:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-056.json:3:  "prompt": "# T-056 — Gate checklist defaults seed\n\nPRD: docs/prd/01-NPD-PRD.md §17.10 + prototype prototypes/design/Monopilot Design System/npd/gate-screens.jsx:14-87 (GATE_CHECKLISTS constant)\nProject root: /Users/mariuszkrawczyk/Projects/monopilot-kira\n\n## Goal\nIdempotent seed populating Reference.GateChecklistTemplates per tenant with the canonical G0-G4 checklist items from the gate-screens.jsx prototype GATE_CHECKLISTS constant — categories technical/business/compliance, required flags preserved.\n\n## Implementation contract\n1. Seed file packages/db/seed/gate-checklist-templates-seed.ts iterates tenants table and INSERTs per-gate items with ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, template_id, gate_code, sequence) DO NOTHING; default template_id='APEX_DEFAULT'.\n2. Items mirror GATE_CHECKLISTS prototype constant (G0=4 items, G1=5 items, G2=6 items, G3=8 items required, G4=6 items required); categories preserved.\n3. Hook into seed orchestrator packages/db/seed/index.ts.\n4. CLI 'pnpm --filter db seed:gate-checklist-templates'.\n\n## Files\n- packages/db/seed/gate-checklist-templates-seed.ts [create]\n- packages/db/seed/index.ts [modify]\n- packages/db/package.json [modify]\n- packages/db/__tests__/gate-checklist-templates-seed.test.ts [create]\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given a fresh DB with one apex tenant, when seed:gate-checklist-templates runs, then 5 gates × N items rows exist (matching GATE_CHECKLISTS counts in prototypes/design/Monopilot Design System/npd/gate-screens.jsx:14-87) per §17.10\n2. Given the seed has already run, when it runs again, then row count is unchanged (idempotent ON CONFLICT)\n3. Given a G3 row exists, when its 'required' flag is queried, then it is TRUE for all 8 items (G3 fully gated per §17.6 approval contract)\n\n## Test strategy\n- RED: integration test asserting per-gate item counts + required flag for G3 + idempotency before seed exists\n- Run 'pnpm --filter db migrate && pnpm --filter db seed:gate-checklist-templates && pnpm --filter db test gate-checklist-templates-seed'\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not deviate from GATE_CHECKLISTS prototype item text (parity required)\n- Do not skip ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING\n- Do not seed only one tenant\n\n## 2026-05-03 E2E spine patch — default G0-G4 gate matrix\nThe seeded checklist templates must explicitly encode the release spine and 7-department closure matrix, not only prototype text. Minimum default template semantics:\n- G0 Idea: brief complete, owner assigned, linked NPD project exists.\n- G1 Feasibility: basic formulation/volume/target launch evidence.\n- G2 Business Case: costing/nutrition/risk initial checks.\n- G3 Development: FG candidate created or mapped (T-095), Trial/Pilot/Packaging evidence placeholders, no blocking risk/docs.\n- G4 Testing/Handoff: required departments Done_<Dept>, RM usability PASS for every BOM component, initial shared BOM ready, initial factory_spec submitted for Technical approval, Settings approval chain complete.\n\nClosed_Technical is not the same as Technical `approved_for_factory`; factory use still requires Technical approval of factory_spec/BOM bundle.",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2679:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-058.json:2:  "title": "T-058 — advanceProjectGate + approveProjectGate (e-sig) + revertGate Server Actions (NPD-f) [PATCH: G3/G4 blockers]",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2680:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-058.json:3:  "prompt": "# T-058 — Gate advancement + approval Server Actions\n\nPRD: docs/prd/01-NPD-PRD.md §17.6, §17.7, §17.12 (adjacency guard)\nProject root: /Users/mariuszkrawczyk/Projects/monopilot-kira\n\n## Goal\nThree Server Actions enforcing gate advancement: advanceProjectGate (G0-G2 self-advance with blocker check), approveProjectGate (G3/G4 with bcrypt-verified password + e-signature SHA-256 hash + audit immutability), revertGate (admin-only audit-logged reverse).\n\n## Implementation contract\n1. apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/advance-project-gate.ts: RBAC npd.gate.advance; calls getBlockers helper; applies adjacency guard nextGate(current) only; updates current_gate; emits 'npd.gate.advanced'.\n2. apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/approve-project-gate.ts: RBAC npd.gate.approve; takes {decision, notes, password}; verifies password via bcrypt against current user; on approve writes gate_approvals row with esigned_at + esign_hash=SHA-256(user_id+project_id+gate+timestamp); advances current_gate; emits 'npd.gate.approved'.\n3. apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/revert-gate.ts: RBAC admin only; writes audit_events; emits 'npd.gate.reverted'.\n4. Vitest covers blocker-rejection, adjacency violation (422 ADJACENCY_VIOLATION), password mismatch reject, hash determinism, and audit-event emission.\n\n## Files\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/advance-project-gate.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/approve-project-gate.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/revert-gate.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/_lib/gate-helpers.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/__tests__/gate-actions.test.ts [create]\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given a project at G2 with one required checklist item not done, when advanceProjectGate to G3 is called, then it rejects with BLOCKERS_PRESENT and current_gate stays G2 per §17.6 blocker rule\n2. Given a project at G2, when advanceProjectGate to G4 (non-adjacent) is called, then it rejects 422 ADJACENCY_VIOLATION per §17.12 adjacency guard\n3. Given approveProjectGate is called with correct password, when commit succeeds, then gate_approvals row contains esign_hash matching SHA-256(user_id + project_id + gate_code + esigned_at) per §17.5 + §17.6 e-sig contract\n\n## Test strategy\n- RED: __tests__/gate-actions.test.ts with 4 cases (blocker reject, adjacency reject, password reject, hash determinism + audit emit) before actions exist\n- Run 'pnpm --filter web test gate-actions'\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not skip blocker check\n- Do not allow non-adjacent advance (per §17.12)\n- Do not store the password in any column or log\n- Do not skip audit_events emission on revertGate\n\n## 2026-05-03 E2E spine patch — G3/G4 advancement blockers\nGate actions must call the E2E blocker helpers added by T-095/T-096/T-097:\n- G3 approval/advance is blocked unless an FG candidate is created or mapped (`npd_projects.product_code` or equivalent) and is unique to this active project.\n- G4 approval is blocked unless required department closures are Done, release preflight passes, RM usability has no blocking FAIL, shared BOM/factory_spec handoff is ready, and Settings policy approvals are satisfied.\n- G4 approval may close NPD, but factory use remains blocked until Technical approval sets the release status/read model to approved/released per T-097.\n- D365 export must not satisfy or mutate any gate blocker.",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2683:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-058.json:31:    "details": "advanceProjectGate enforces blocker + adjacency. approveProjectGate verifies password via bcrypt then writes gate_approvals + esign_hash. revertGate is admin-only and audit-logged. Helper getBlockers + nextGate factored.\nPreserved acceptance requirements: Given a project at G2 with no FG candidate, when approve/advance to G3 is called, then it rejects with FG_CANDIDATE_REQUIRED.; Given a project at G3 with any required department not Done, when approveProjectGate for G4 is called, then it rejects with DEPARTMENT_CLOSURE_REQUIRED and typed blockers.; Given D365 export exists but Technical approval is missing, when factory release blockers are evaluated, then the project is not released_to_factory.",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2685:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-058.json:54:      "Given a project at G2, when advanceProjectGate to G4 (non-adjacent) is called, then it rejects 422 ADJACENCY_VIOLATION per §17.12 adjacency guard",
_meta/plans/2026-07-16-sol-fix-campaign/waveW1/R4/out/REVIEW4-codex.err:2686:_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-059.json:3:  "prompt": "# T-059 — Pipeline Kanban view UI\n\nPRD: docs/prd/01-NPD-PRD.md §17.8, §17.12 + UX prototypes/design/01-NPD-UX.md pipeline_kanban\nProject root: /Users/mariuszkrawczyk/Projects/monopilot-kira\nPrototype: prototypes/design/Monopilot Design System/npd/pipeline.jsx:19-52 (KanbanCard + KanbanView)\n\n## Goal\nClient component KanbanView rendering 6 columns (G0-G4 + Launched) with project cards, drag-and-drop adjacency-guarded via @dnd-kit/core, optimistic UI revert on 422 ADJACENCY_VIOLATION. Mounted at /(npd)/pipeline?view=kanban (default).\n\n## Implementation contract\n1. apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_components/kanban-view.tsx ('use client') uses @dnd-kit/core; renders shadcn Card per project; column header per gate with count.\n2. onDragEnd calls advanceProjectGate(projectId, targetGate) — optimistic update + rollback on error.\n3. Card content matches prototype: code, name, prio badge, owner, target_launch.\n4. RTL test asserts 6 columns + card rendering + DnD adjacency rejection (mock action returns 422).\n\n## Files\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/page.tsx [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_components/kanban-view.tsx [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_components/kanban-card.tsx [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_components/__tests__/kanban-view.test.tsx [create]\n- prototypes/design/Monopilot Design System/npd/pipeline.jsx [ref]\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given the production page renders, when compared to prototypes/design/Monopilot Design System/npd/pipeline.jsx:19-52 (KanbanCard + KanbanView), then it has 6 gate columns (G0,G1,G2,G3,G4,Launched), KanbanCard with code+name+prio badge+owner+target_launch, and uses @dnd-kit/core + shadcn Card primitives — verified by RTL snapshot + parity checklist\n2. Given a card is dragged from G2 to G3 (adjacent), when drop fires, then advanceProjectGate is invoked with targetGate=G3 and UI updates optimistically per §17.12 adjacency rule\n3. Given the action returns 422 ADJACENCY_VIOLATION, when the drop completes, then the card snaps back to its source column and a toast shows the error per §17.12 optimistic-revert contract\n\n## Test strategy\n- RED: RTL test asserting 6 columns + card content + DnD adjacent + 422 revert before component exists\n- Run 'pnpm --filter web test kanban-view'\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not allow non-adjacent drop without server validation\n- Do not paste prototype JSX verbatim — translate to @dnd-kit + shadcn\n- Do not skip optimistic revert UX",
