Given a project at G2, when advanceProjectGate to G4 (non-adjacent) is called, then it rejects 422 ADJACENCY_VIOLATION per §17.12 adjacency guard\n3. Given approveProjectGate is called with correct password, when commit succeeds, then gate_approvals row contains esign_hash matching SHA-256(user_id + project_id + gate_code + esigned_at) per §17.5 + §17.6 e-sig contract\n\n## Test strategy\n- RED: __tests__/gate-actions.test.ts with 4 cases (blocker reject, adjacency reject, password reject, hash determinism + audit emit) before actions exist\n- Run 'pnpm --filter web test gate-actions'\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not skip blocker check\n- Do not allow non-adjacent advance (per §17.12)\n- Do not store the password in any column or log\n- Do not skip audit_events emission on revertGate\n\n## 2026-05-03 E2E spine patch — G3/G4 advancement blockers\nGate actions must call the E2E blocker helpers added by T-095/T-096/T-097:\n- G3 approval/advance is blocked unless an FG candidate is created or mapped (`npd_projects.product_code` or equivalent) and is unique to this active project.\n- G4 approval is blocked unless required department closures are Done, release preflight passes, RM usability has no blocking FAIL, shared BOM/factory_spec handoff is ready, and Settings policy approvals are satisfied.\n- G4 approval may close NPD, but factory use remains blocked until Technical approval sets the release status/read model to approved/released per T-097.\n- D365 export must not satisfy or mutate any gate blocker.",
