_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-058.json:3:  "prompt": "# T-058 — Gate advancement + approval Server Actions\n\nPRD: docs/prd/01-NPD-PRD.md §17.6, §17.7, §17.12 (adjacency guard)\nProject root: /Users/mariuszkrawczyk/Projects/monopilot-kira\n\n## Goal\nThree Server Actions enforcing gate advancement: advanceProjectGate (G0-G2 self-advance with blocker check), approveProjectGate (G3/G4 with bcrypt-verified password + e-signature SHA-256 hash + audit immutability), revertGate (admin-only audit-logged reverse).\n\n## Implementation contract\n1. apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/advance-project-gate.ts: RBAC npd.gate.advance; calls getBlockers helper; applies adjacency guard nextGate(current) only; updates current_gate; emits 'npd.gate.advanced'.\n2. apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/approve-project-gate.ts: RBAC npd.gate.approve; takes {decision, notes, password}; verifies password via bcrypt against current user; on approve writes gate_approvals row with esigned_at + esign_hash=SHA-256(user_id+project_id+gate+timestamp); advances current_gate; emits 'npd.gate.approved'.\n3. apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/revert-gate.ts: RBAC admin only; writes audit_events; emits 'npd.gate.reverted'.\n4. Vitest covers blocker-rejection, adjacency violation (422 ADJACENCY_VIOLATION), password mismatch reject, hash determinism, and audit-event emission.\n\n## Files\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/advance-project-gate.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/approve-project-gate.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/revert-gate.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/_lib/gate-helpers.ts [create]\n- apps/web/app/(npd)/pipeline/_actions/__tests__/gate-actions.test.ts [create]\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given a project at G2 with one required checklist item not done, when advanceProjectGate to G3 is called, then it rejects with BLOCKERS_PRESENT and current_gate stays G2 per §17.6 blocker rule\n2. Given a project at G2, when advanceProjectGate to G4 (non-adjacent) is called, then it rejects 422 ADJACENCY_VIOLATION per §17.12 adjacency guard\n3. Given approveProjectGate is called with correct password, when commit succeeds, then gate_approvals row contains esign_hash matching SHA-256(user_id + project_id + gate_code + esigned_at) per §17.5 + §17.6 e-sig contract\n\n## Test strategy\n- RED: __tests__/gate-actions.test.ts with 4 cases (blocker reject, adjacency reject, password reject, hash determinism + audit emit) before actions exist\n- Run 'pnpm --filter web test gate-actions'\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not skip blocker check\n- Do not allow non-adjacent advance (per §17.12)\n- Do not store the password in any column or log\n- Do not skip audit_events emission on revertGate\n\n## 2026-05-03 E2E spine patch — G3/G4 advancement blockers\nGate actions must call the E2E blocker helpers added by T-095/T-096/T-097:\n- G3 approval/advance is blocked unless an FG candidate is created or mapped (`npd_projects.product_code` or equivalent) and is unique to this active project.\n- G4 approval is blocked unless required department closures are Done, release preflight passes, RM usability has no blocking FAIL, shared BOM/factory_spec handoff is ready, and Settings policy approvals are satisfied.\n- G4 approval may close NPD, but factory use remains blocked until Technical approval sets the release status/read model to approved/released per T-097.\n- D365 export must not satisfy or mutate any gate blocker.",
_meta/atomic-tasks/01-npd/tasks/T-058.json:31:    "details": "advanceProjectGate enforces blocker + adjacency. approveProjectGate verifies password via bcrypt then writes gate_approvals + esign_hash. revertGate is admin-only and audit-logged. Helper getBlockers + nextGate factored.\nPreserved acceptance requirements: Given a project at G2 with no FG candidate, when approve/advance to G3 is called, then it rejects with FG_CANDIDATE_REQUIRED.; Given a project at G3 with any required department not Done, when approveProjectGate for G4 is called, then it rejects with DEPARTMENT_CLOSURE_REQUIRED and typed blockers.; Given D365 export exists but Technical approval is missing, when factory release blockers are evaluated, then the project is not released_to_factory.",
